## 2. Direct Official Vertex AI OpenAPI-Compatible Endpoint (Zero-Proxy)

Google Cloud Vertex AI natively exposes an OpenAI-compatible `/chat/completions` REST interface. This completely eliminates the need to run LiteLLM or an intermediate proxy process.

### 2.1 Endpoint URL & Base URL Structure (`global` vs Regional)
- **Canonical Global Base URL for OpenAI SDK (Recommended Default)**:
  `https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/{PROJECT_ID}/locations/global/endpoints/openapi`
- **Regional Base URL (Legacy / Region-Locked Models Only)**:
  `https://{LOCATION}-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/{PROJECT_ID}/locations/{LOCATION}/endpoints/openapi`
- **Full Completions Path**:
  `POST https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/{PROJECT_ID}/locations/global/endpoints/openapi/chat/completions`
- **Critical Routing Rule (`global` vs `us-central1`)**:
  - Models in the **Gemini 3** (`google/gemini-3-flash-preview`, `google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview`) and **Gemini 4** (`google/gemini-4-argon`) families are published on the **`global`** location (`locations/global`). Calling them against `us-central1-aiplatform.googleapis.com/.../locations/us-central1` fails with HTTP `404 Publisher model ... was not found`.
  - When `location === 'global'`, the hostname MUST be bare `aiplatform.googleapis.com` (never `global-aiplatform.googleapis.com`):
    ```ts
    const host = location === 'global' ? 'aiplatform.googleapis.com' : `${location}-aiplatform.googleapis.com`;
    const baseUrl = `https://${host}/v1beta1/projects/${projectId}/locations/${location}/endpoints/openapi`;
    ```
  - Always normalize legacy regional URLs in saved DB configs or auto-retry against `locations/global` when a regional Vertex endpoint returns `404 NOT_FOUND`.

### 2.2 Multi-Tier Token Refresh & Introspection Algorithm
Google OAuth2 access tokens (`ya29.*`) expire every 60 minutes (3600s). A resilient backend should implement a **3-tier token resolution ladder** combined with **proactive 50-minute caching**, **tokeninfo TTL introspection**, and **reactive 401/403 self-healing**:

1. **Tier 1 — Active `gcloud` CLI Account**:
   Run `gcloud auth print-access-token [account]` (with explicit `/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin` in `PATH` so GUI/daemon processes find the binary).
2. **Tier 2 — Direct OAuth2 Refresh Token Exchange (ADC Fallback)**:
   Read `~/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json` (`client_id`, `client_secret`, `refresh_token`) and `POST https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token` with `grant_type=refresh_token`. Works even if `gcloud` CLI is slow or unavailable.
3. **Tier 3 — Environment Variable Override**:
   Fallback to `process.env.VERTEX_TOKEN || process.env.VERTEX_API_KEY`.
4. **Token Introspection (`tokeninfo`)**:
   Query `GET https://oauth2.googleapis.com/tokeninfo?access_token=<token>` to verify the exact remaining `expires_in` seconds and authenticated `email`, setting `expiresAt = Date.now() + expiresInSec * 1000` with a 5-minute safety window (`REFRESH_SAFETY_WINDOW_MS = 5 * 60 * 1000`).
5. **Reactive 401/403 Self-Healing Retry in Streaming Pipelines**:
   In the LLM streaming caller, if Vertex AI returns HTTP `401`, `403`, or `UNAUTHENTICATED` before tokens are emitted, call `await refreshVertexTokenAsync(true)` to force-invalidate the cached token and transparently replay the request once (`_retriedVertexAuth = true`).

### 2.3 Model Naming & Thinking Token Pitfalls
- **Mandatory `google/` Prefix**: Model names on the OpenAPI endpoint must include the vendor prefix:
  - `google/gemini-2.5-flash`
  - `google/gemini-2.5-pro`
  - `google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite`
  - `google/gemini-3.8-flash`
  - `google/gemini-3.7-flash`
  - `google/gemini-4-argon`
  Calling bare `gemini-2.5-flash` without `google/` returns HTTP 400 `Invalid model name`.
- **Reasoning Tokens (Thinking Budget)**: Gemini 2.5+ models stream `reasoning_content` tokens prior to answering. Always ensure `max_tokens` is configured ≥ 1024; setting small `max_tokens` (e.g. 100–300) causes the model to consume the entire quota on internal reasoning, yielding empty final replies.
- **Gemini 3.7+ Thinking Budget for Conversational Latency**: By default, `gemini-3.7-flash` enables dynamic reasoning tokens which can stall interactive chat turns for 80+ seconds. For low-latency conversational and agentic workflows, explicitly disable or clamp thinking via REST `generationConfig.thinkingConfig = { thinkingBudget: 0 }` (or `thinkingBudget: 1024`). Setting `thinkingBudget: 0` drops turn latency from ~85s to ~2.9s while preserving high quality.

### 2.4 In-App Browser OAuth Login & Multi-Account Switching
To let users log in or switch Google Cloud accounts directly from a web settings UI:
- **List Accounts**: `gcloud auth list --format=json` returns `[{ account, status: "ACTIVE" | "" }]`.
- **Switch Active Account**: `gcloud config set account <email>` followed by forced token refresh (`refreshVertexTokenAsync(true)`).
- **Trigger Browser OAuth Flow**: Spawn `gcloud auth login --launch-browser --brief` (and optionally `gcloud auth application-default login` when `adc: true`) in the background (`detached: true`), and poll `gcloud auth list` or wait for process exit `code === 0` to automatically refresh the cached token.

### 2.5 Dynamic Vertex AI Model Discovery & Regional Endpoint Pitfall
- **Regional Endpoint Pitfall (HTTP 404)**: Calling `GET https://us-central1-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/publishers/google/models` returns `404 Not Found` on standard GCP projects.
- **Global Publisher Models Endpoint (HTTP 200)**: Always query the **global** endpoint with the project billed via `x-goog-user-project`:
  ```http
  GET https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/publishers/google/models?pageSize=100
  Authorization: Bearer <VERTEX_OAUTH_TOKEN>
  x-goog-user-project: <GCP_PROJECT_ID>
  ```
  Filter `publisherModels` where `name` matches `/^publishers\/google\/models\/gemini-[a-z0-9.-]+$/`, prefix each ID with `google/`, and merge with a curated fallback catalog so UI model selectors remain populated even offline.

### 2.6 Preserving Gemini 3 & Gemini 4 `thought_signature` in Multi-Turn Tool Loops
When invoking tools (`tool_calls`) with **Gemini 3** (`google/gemini-3-flash-preview`, `google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview`) or **Gemini 4** (`google/gemini-4-argon`) on the Vertex AI OpenAI-compatible endpoint, Vertex emits a cryptographic `thought_signature` inside each streamed tool-call delta:
```json
{
  "index": 0,
  "id": "0",
  "type": "function",
  "function": { "name": "read_workspace_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"pyproject.toml\"}" },
  "extra_content": {
    "google": {
      "thought_signature": "<base64_signature>"
    }
  }
}
```
- **The Pitfall (`400 INVALID_ARGUMENT`)**: Standard OpenAI-compatible client libraries (such as `@earendil-works/pi-ai` and OpenAI's message normalizers) construct the Turn 2 `assistant` message with `{ id, type, function }` and strip unknown fields like `extra_content`. On Turn 2, Vertex AI rejects the request with:
  `400 Function call is missing a thought_signature in functionCall parts.`
- **The Solution (`onProviderStreamEvent` + `onPayload` Hook Bridge)**:
  Capture `tc.extra_content` from raw provider SSE chunks during Turn 1 and re-attach it to `msg.tool_calls` in `onPayload` before Turn 2 is transmitted:
  ```ts
  const toolCallExtraById = new Map<string, Record<string, unknown>>();
  const toolCallExtraByIndex = new Map<number, Record<string, unknown>>();
  let latestExtraContent: Record<string, unknown> | undefined;

  // 1. Capture extra_content.google.thought_signature from raw SSE chunks:
  onProviderStreamEvent: (chunk: unknown) => {
    const c = chunk as { choices?: Array<{ delta?: { tool_calls?: Array<Record<string, unknown>> } }> };
    const tcs = c?.choices?.[0]?.delta?.tool_calls;
    if (!Array.isArray(tcs)) return;
    for (const tc of tcs) {
      const extra = tc.extra_content as Record<string, unknown> | undefined;
      if (extra && typeof extra === 'object') {
        latestExtraContent = extra;
        if (typeof tc.index === 'number') toolCallExtraByIndex.set(tc.index, extra);
        if (typeof tc.id === 'string' && tc.id) toolCallExtraById.set(tc.id, extra);
      } else if (typeof tc.id === 'string' && tc.id && typeof tc.index === 'number') {
        const byIdx = toolCallExtraByIndex.get(tc.index);
        if (byIdx) toolCallExtraById.set(tc.id, byIdx);
      }
    }
  },

  // 2. Re-inject extra_content onto assistant.tool_calls on subsequent turns:
    onPayload: (payload: unknown) => {
      const p = payload as { messages?: Array<Record<string, unknown>> };
      if (!p || !Array.isArray(p.messages)) return payload;
      for (const msg of p.messages) {
        if (msg.role === 'assistant' && Array.isArray(msg.tool_calls)) {
          (msg.tool_calls as Array<Record<string, unknown>>).forEach((tc, idx) => {
            if (!tc.extra_content) {
              const extra =
                (typeof tc.id === 'string' ? toolCallExtraById.get(tc.id) : undefined) ??
                toolCallExtraByIndex.get(idx) ??
                latestExtraContent;
              if (extra) tc.extra_content = extra;
            }
          });
        }
      }
      return payload;
    }
  ```

### 2.7 URL Normalization Pitfall: Version Regex `/v1beta1` Truncation (HTTP 404)
Standard OpenAI-compatible proxies and SDK client normalizers often detect API versions using naive regexes:
```ts
// DANGEROUS: Matches only pure digits like /v1/ or /v2/
const hasVersion = /\/v\d+(?:\/|$)/.test(url);
if (!hasVersion) url += '/v1/chat/completions';
```
- **The Pitfall**: For Google Cloud Vertex AI OpenAPI endpoints (`https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/.../endpoints/openapi`), `/\v\d+(?:\/|$)/` fails to match `/v1beta1` because of the trailing `beta1`. The normalizer mistakenly strips the endpoint path or appends `/v1/chat/completions`, hitting `https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/chat/completions` which yields:
  `404 Not Found: upstream error`
- **The Fix**: Use an alphanumeric-aware version regex:
  ```ts
  const hasVersion = /\/v\d+[a-z0-9]*(?:\/|$)/i.test(url);
  ```
  And when constructing the full chat URL, only append `/chat/completions` if the path doesn't already terminate with it.

### 2.8 BYOK & Streaming Proxy Sentinel Key Pattern (`CONNECTED_VIA_GCLOUD`)
In desktop or web apps supporting Bring-Your-Own-Key (BYOK) runtimes (such as OpenCode or custom streaming proxies):
- Raw OAuth2 Bearer tokens (`ya29.*`) expire hourly and should never be persisted in localStorage or client database config.
- **Sentinel Key Convention**: Set `apiKey: 'CONNECTED_VIA_GCLOUD'` (or `gcloud`) in client config.
- The daemon proxy interceptor checks `if (apiKey === 'CONNECTED_VIA_GCLOUD' || isVertexHost(baseUrl))`:
  1. Dynamically fetches or refreshes the OAuth2 token (`getCachedToken()` / `refreshVertexTokenAsync()`).
  2. Injects the Bearer header: `headers['Authorization'] = `Bearer ${token}``.
  3. Validates that downstream execution engines do not fail on "missing API key" validation checks.


