## 3. Local OpenAI-to-Vertex Gateway (LiteLLM)

### 3.1 Authentication via Application Default Credentials (ADC) & Quota Project
Ensure local gcloud credentials are active and quota project is configured:
```bash
gcloud auth application-default login
gcloud config set project <YOUR_GCP_PROJECT_ID>
gcloud auth application-default set-quota-project <YOUR_GCP_PROJECT_ID>
```

> [!WARNING] ADC Quota Project Pitfall (HTTP 403 PERMISSION_DENIED)
> Calling Google Cloud APIs (such as `texttospeech.googleapis.com` or Vertex AI client libraries) using local ADC without a configured quota project fails with:
> `Your application is authenticating by using local Application Default Credentials. The texttospeech.googleapis.com API requires a quota project, which is not set by default.`
> Running `gcloud auth application-default set-quota-project <PROJECT_ID>` writes `"quota_project_id": "<PROJECT_ID>"` into `~/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json`, resolving the error permanently for all client libraries. For raw curl/HTTP requests, also supply `-H "x-goog-user-project: <PROJECT_ID>"`.

### 3.2 Configuration (`litellm_config.yaml`)
```yaml
model_list:
  - model_name: gpt-4o
    litellm_params:
      model: vertex_ai/gemini-2.5-pro
      vertex_project: "<YOUR_GCP_PROJECT_ID>"
      vertex_location: "us-central1"
  - model_name: gpt-4o-mini
    litellm_params:
      model: vertex_ai/gemini-2.5-flash
      vertex_project: "<YOUR_GCP_PROJECT_ID>"
      vertex_location: "us-central1"
  - model_name: text-embedding-3-small
    litellm_params:
      model: vertex_ai/text-embedding-004
      vertex_project: "<YOUR_GCP_PROJECT_ID>"
      vertex_location: "us-central1"

general_settings:
  master_key: "sk-local-gcp-bridge"
```

### 3.3 Starting the Local Daemon
```bash
litellm --config litellm_config.yaml --port 4000 --host 127.0.0.1
```

Point any CLI agent or client (AgentsRoom, Cursor, Aider, OpenCode):
- `OPENAI_BASE_URL`: `http://127.0.0.1:4000/v1`
- `OPENAI_API_KEY`: `sk-local-gcp-bridge`

